  "instrument": "TMA1995",
  "kind": "section",
  "number": "202",
  "ref": "TMA1995/s202",
  "text": "The Registrar may, for the purposes of this Act: (a) summon witnesses; and (b) receive written or oral evidence on oath or affirmation; and (c) require the production of documents or articles; and (d) award costs against a party to proceedings brought before the Registrar; and (e) notify any person of any matter that, in his or her opinion, should be brought to the person’s notice. Note: For the awarding of costs see section 221.",
